Design: I propose replacing the per‐epoch CosineAnnealingLR schedule with a batch‐wise OneCycleLR scheduler and increasing to 5 training epochs. OneCycleLR dynamically adjusts the learning rate each batch to improve generalization, and more epochs give the scheduler room to vary the LR, which often boosts AUROC. This change is atomic and only modifies the optimizer/scheduler setup and training loop. The rest of the pipeline, including weighted sampling for skin tones, focal loss, TTA, and 5‐fold CV, remains unchanged.
